  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: province</p>\r\n<p>Cappadocia was garrisoned with Roman auxiliary soldiers and was placed under the administrative control of a procurator. It was joined with Cappadocia under Cn. Domitius Corbulo (55-61 and 63-65/66) and L. Iunius Caesennius Paetus (61-63).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Galatia et Cappadocia, a Roman province that results from the union of Galatia and Cappadocia.",
